130
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:16,200
My mom gave me this guitar when I was a kid.

131
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,720
She's the one who taught me how to play.

132
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:21,640
My mom also taught me a really cool way to play,

133
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,840
which is playing while lying down.

134
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,360
Why?

135
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,800
Because she said that

136
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,880
playing standing up for too long hurts your back,

137
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:32,120
playing sitting down hurts your shoulders,

138
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:34,040
and only playing lying down is the most comfortable

139
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,970
and effortless.

140
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,840
When I was with my mom,

141
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,240
no matter how naughty I was,

142
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,720
she would never stop me.

143
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:42,280
But my dad would get very angry when he saw it,

144
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,880
and he would scold me every time.

145
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:44,920
As soon as I saw my dad was about to scold me,

146
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,780
I would immediately run to my mom.

147
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:49,810
And then I would learn to play the guitar with her.

148
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,610
This way, when my dad saw

149
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:53,520
that I was learning the guitar,

150
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,180
he wouldn't scold me anymore.

151
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:57,280
Then my mom would teach me how to hum a song.

152
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:59,480
We would hum for a long, long time,

153
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,610
and her voice would get softer and softer.

154
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:04,680
Then my mom would give me money to buy candy.

155
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,840
I would go out to play for a while

156
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:06,970
before coming back.

157
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,000
When I came back, I found that

158
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,810
my mom was full of energy again.

159
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,680
When I was a kid, I always wondered

160
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:15,640
why

161
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,660
my mom didn't live in the same house as us.

162
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,320
Later, I found out

163
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:23,760
that my mom

164
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,880
was seriously ill.

165
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:31,480
Even then,

166
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,240
she would, every day,

167
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:36,370
teach me to play the guitar,

168
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:37,740
because

169
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,250
she wanted to pass on

170
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,409
the thing she loved most

171
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,520
to me, the one she loved most.

172
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:52,880
Later,

173
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:56,720
I took the first chord she taught me

174
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,659
and turned it into a complete single.

175
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,800
That was also my debut single.

176
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,770
Are my requirements for him

177
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,000
